# Cloudflare Pages response headers. The export copies this file into out/.
#
# Every path gets the security headers. None of them changes what a page may
# load, only how the browser may treat it. Content-Security-Policy is
# deliberately absent: framer-motion writes inline styles on every animated
# element and rapier instantiates WebAssembly, so a policy needs at least
# style-src 'unsafe-inline' and a wasm source, and a wrong one silently blanks
# the experience. It needs a report-only rollout against the live site first.
# HSTS has no includeSubDomains and no preload, because neither is reversible
# on a timescale a portfolio can afford.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000

# The generated images are written as files with no extension, and Pages takes
# Content-Type from the extension, so without these rules they go out as
# application/octet-stream and link unfurlers refuse them. The cache stays
# short because pages reference these URLs without a build hash in the path,
# and a long one would pin a stale card in unfurler caches after a deploy.
/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/cinematic/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/play/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/projects/opengraph-image
  Content-Type: image/jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/icon
  Content-Type: image/png
/apple-icon
  Content-Type: image/png
